                                            "To endure primitive conditions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41c6b06d-fe7e-4bcd-9e65-31e4f341e00a",
                                                "sense_id": "2b323c93-4bab-3b35-8bf9-550ef13d0a54",
                                                "text": "to rough it"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e07731e8-2611-484b-8932-31f73d83e9da",
                                                "sense_id": "2b323c93-4bab-3b35-8bf9-550ef13d0a54",
                                                "text": "“[…]Oh, but my husband is never so happy as when he is travelling. He likes roughing it. . . . My husband. . . . My husband. . . .”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6980067c-168b-4cd4-8881-d14b17016ac3",
                                                "sense_id": "2b323c93-4bab-3b35-8bf9-550ef13d0a54",
                                                "text": "I was able to help Trudy set up camp and everything else, of course there are different ways to camp the usual comfortable way or roughed we of course roughed it and I did my best to keep warm."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
